A||||3||Homicidal||Clutch won't DEPRESS? Can't shift at all!!!!!! ||||8||
Z||000000||Homicidal||04-19-2000||02:33 AM||||I was coming back from LA down to San Diego (where else!) when I hit some traffic and had to slow down. I<BR>                          downshifted to first since I had to stop and started off again, but when I shifted into 3rd gear my clutch stuck a<BR>                          little and the gears grinded. When I finally got into 3rd my clutch pedal locked up and I couldn't press it down to<BR>                          shift anymore! I managed to get across 3-4 lanes and get off the freeway into a parking lot.<P>                          Now my car won't start because I cannot press the clutch down to make it start! It's like it has a brick underneath<BR>                          it or something! What's wrong with my car? Why did it lock up so quickly and suddenly?<BR>||||reg||8
Z||000001||WKDFIRO||04-19-2000||02:39 AM||||Sounds like the clutch just went out. The clutch fork has probably been tweeked and jammed up on you. Usually its just the clutch that goes before any damage to the tranny occurs. <P>Unless you have a trusted mechanic already or you want to do it yourself you can call Fiero Motorsports in Orange. (Yes its a shameless plug!) 714 639-9005. Tell Keith that Anthony sent ya!||||reg||9
Z||000002||WKDFIRO||04-20-2000||03:47 AM||||Another possiblility (after talking with the Fiero Doc) is that the clutch lever may have come off. If the piston at the slave cylinder has nothing to push when you push the clutch pedal it will go all the way out. If you still have a return spring on your clutch pedal it will return the pedal up. Trying to force the clutch pedal down would blow the seals in the slave! Hope this isn't too late!||||reg||11
Z||000003||Homicidal||04-20-2000||03:52 AM||||Nah, it's still in the up position.  Just won't budge more than an inch or 2 before it "stiffens" and you can't push it anymore.<P>I didn't try forcing it down as I would see no good direct result of it besides busting the clutch or getting it stuck in the down position.<P>||||reg||1
